# MAGIC <div class="dbx">
# MAGIC <div class="sec-head"><span class="sec-num">03</span><span class="sec-icon">⚠️</span><h2>The classic trap: average of averages</h2></div><p>Imagine a standard view pre-aggregated per <strong>category × month</strong>:</p>
# MAGIC <div class="code"><div class="code-bar"><i></i><i></i><i></i><span class="lang">SQL</span><button class="copy" type="button">copy</button></div><pre><span style="color: #FF7B72">CREATE</span><span style="color: #6E7681"> </span><span style="color: #FF7B72">VIEW</span><span style="color: #6E7681"> </span><span style="color: #E6EDF3">v_sales_by_category_month</span><span style="color: #6E7681"> </span><span style="color: #FF7B72">AS</span>
# MAGIC <span style="color: #FF7B72">SELECT</span><span style="color: #6E7681"> </span><span style="color: #E6EDF3">product_category,</span><span style="color: #6E7681"> </span><span style="color: #E6EDF3">order_month,</span>
# MAGIC <span style="color: #6E7681">       </span><span style="color: #FF7B72">SUM</span><span style="color: #E6EDF3">(net_revenue)</span><span style="color: #6E7681"> </span><span style="color: #FF7B72; font-weight: bold">/</span><span style="color: #6E7681"> </span><span style="color: #FF7B72">COUNT</span><span style="color: #E6EDF3">(</span><span style="color: #FF7B72; font-weight: bold">*</span><span style="color: #E6EDF3">)</span><span style="color: #6E7681">  </span><span style="color: #FF7B72">AS</span><span style="color: #6E7681"> </span><span style="color: #E6EDF3">avg_order_value,</span>
# MAGIC <span style="color: #6E7681">       </span><span style="color: #FF7B72">COUNT</span><span style="color: #E6EDF3">(</span><span style="color: #FF7B72">DISTINCT</span><span style="color: #6E7681"> </span><span style="color: #E6EDF3">customer_id)</span><span style="color: #6E7681">  </span><span style="color: #FF7B72">AS</span><span style="color: #6E7681"> </span><span style="color: #E6EDF3">unique_customers</span>
# MAGIC <span style="color: #FF7B72">FROM</span><span style="color: #6E7681"> </span><span style="color: #E6EDF3">orders</span><span style="color: #6E7681"> </span><span style="color: #FF7B72">GROUP</span><span style="color: #6E7681"> </span><span style="color: #FF7B72">BY</span><span style="color: #6E7681"> </span><span style="color: #FF7B72">ALL</span><span style="color: #E6EDF3">;</span></pre></div>
# MAGIC <p>Now someone (or Genie) asks <em>"What was the average order value and number of customers in 2025?"</em></p>
# MAGIC <ul>
# MAGIC <li><code>AVG(avg_order_value)</code> → <strong>wrong</strong> (averages of averages ignore the order volume behind each value)</li>
# MAGIC <li><code>SUM(unique_customers)</code> → <strong>wrong</strong> (the same customer is counted in many months and categories)</li>
# MAGIC </ul>
# MAGIC <p>With a metric view, <code>MEASURE(avg_order_value)</code> and <code>MEASURE(unique_customers)</code> are <strong>re-computed from the detail rows at whatever grain you ask for</strong>: year, category, region, or nothing at all.</p>
# MAGIC <blockquote class="callout">
# MAGIC <p>The hands-on demo notebook reproduces this with real numbers.</p>
# MAGIC </blockquote>
# MAGIC </div>

