# MAGIC <div class="sec-head"><span class="sec-num">05</span><span class="sec-icon">📏</span><h2>Creating a metric view</h2></div><p>Three ways to create one:</p>
# MAGIC <ol>
# MAGIC <li><strong>SQL DDL</strong>: <code>CREATE OR REPLACE VIEW … WITH METRICS LANGUAGE YAML AS &#36;&#36; … &#36;&#36;</code></li>
# MAGIC <li><strong>Catalog Explorer UI</strong>: open a table → <strong>Create → Metric view</strong>. The visual editor offers joins, filters, fields, measures, <em>Preview</em>, and a <code>&lt;&gt;</code> YAML tab.</li>
# MAGIC <li><strong>Genie Code</strong>: describe the metric view in natural language, or import Tableau / Power BI definitions.</li>
# MAGIC </ol>
# MAGIC <div class="code"><div class="code-bar"><i></i><i></i><i></i><span class="lang">SQL</span><button class="copy" type="button">copy</button></div><pre><span style="color: #FF7B72">CREATE</span><span style="color: #6E7681"> </span><span style="color: #FF7B72">OR</span><span style="color: #6E7681"> </span><span style="color: #FF7B72">REPLACE</span><span style="color: #6E7681"> </span><span style="color: #FF7B72">VIEW</span><span style="color: #6E7681"> </span><span style="color: #E6EDF3">sales_metrics</span>
# MAGIC <span style="color: #FF7B72">WITH</span><span style="color: #6E7681"> </span><span style="color: #E6EDF3">METRICS</span>
# MAGIC <span style="color: #FF7B72">LANGUAGE</span><span style="color: #6E7681"> </span><span style="color: #E6EDF3">YAML</span>
# MAGIC <span style="color: #FF7B72">AS</span><span style="color: #6E7681"> </span><span style="color: #F85149">&#36;&#36;</span>
# MAGIC <span style="color: #FF7B72">version</span><span style="color: #E6EDF3">:</span><span style="color: #6E7681"> </span><span style="color: #A5D6FF">1</span><span style="color: #E6EDF3">.</span><span style="color: #A5D6FF">1</span>
# MAGIC <span style="color: #FF7B72">source</span><span style="color: #E6EDF3">:</span><span style="color: #6E7681"> </span><span style="color: #E6EDF3">main.retail.fact_orders</span>
# MAGIC <span style="color: #E6EDF3">fields:</span>
# MAGIC <span style="color: #6E7681">  </span><span style="color: #FF7B72; font-weight: bold">-</span><span style="color: #6E7681"> </span><span style="color: #E6EDF3">name:</span><span style="color: #6E7681"> </span><span style="color: #E6EDF3">order_month</span>
# MAGIC <span style="color: #6E7681">    </span><span style="color: #E6EDF3">expr:</span><span style="color: #6E7681"> </span><span style="color: #E6EDF3">DATE_TRUNC(</span><span style="color: #A5D6FF">'MONTH'</span><span style="color: #E6EDF3">,</span><span style="color: #6E7681"> </span><span style="color: #E6EDF3">order_date)</span>
# MAGIC <span style="color: #E6EDF3">measures:</span>
# MAGIC <span style="color: #6E7681">  </span><span style="color: #FF7B72; font-weight: bold">-</span><span style="color: #6E7681"> </span><span style="color: #E6EDF3">name:</span><span style="color: #6E7681"> </span><span style="color: #E6EDF3">order_count</span>
# MAGIC <span style="color: #6E7681">    </span><span style="color: #E6EDF3">expr:</span><span style="color: #6E7681"> </span><span style="color: #FF7B72">COUNT</span><span style="color: #E6EDF3">(</span><span style="color: #A5D6FF">1</span><span style="color: #E6EDF3">)</span>
# MAGIC <span style="color: #F85149">&#36;&#36;</span><span style="color: #E6EDF3">;</span></pre></div>
# MAGIC <p><strong>Privileges needed:</strong> <code>SELECT</code> on the sources, <code>USE CATALOG</code>, plus <code>USE SCHEMA</code> and <code>CREATE TABLE</code> on the target schema, and access to a SQL warehouse or compute on a supported runtime.</p>
# MAGIC </div>

