# MAGIC <div class="dbx">
# MAGIC <div class="sec-head"><span class="sec-num">14</span><span class="sec-icon">🏆</span><h2>Best practices</h2></div><ul>
# MAGIC <li><strong>Name for humans and LLMs:</strong> <code>net_revenue</code>, not <code>m_rev_2</code>, plus <code>display_name</code> and <code>synonyms</code>.</li>
# MAGIC <li><strong>Put business rules in the definition:</strong> global <code>filter</code> for exclusions (test data), <code>FILTER (WHERE …)</code> for measure-level rules.</li>
# MAGIC <li><strong>Prefer ratio measures composed from base measures.</strong> Never pre-aggregate ratios.</li>
# MAGIC <li><strong>Declare PK/FK constraints with <code>RELY</code></strong> on source tables. Genie and the optimizer both benefit.</li>
# MAGIC <li><strong>Comment everything:</strong> comments are the cheapest accuracy boost for Genie.</li>
# MAGIC <li><strong>One metric view per business process</strong> (sales, support tickets, inventory), not one giant view.</li>
# MAGIC <li><strong>Version control:</strong> keep the YAML in Git and deploy with SQL / Databricks Asset Bundles.</li>
# MAGIC </ul>
# MAGIC </div>

