# MAGIC <div class="dbx">
# MAGIC <div class="sec-head"><span class="sec-num">15</span><span class="sec-icon">🎓</span><h2>Trainer notes: questions learners ask</h2></div><ul>
# MAGIC <li><strong>"Isn't this just a view?"</strong> No. A view fixes the GROUP BY, while a metric view lets the query decide it and still computes non-additive measures correctly.</li>
# MAGIC <li><strong>"Do I still need Genie instructions?"</strong> Yes, but fewer. Use them for business context and terminology, and put formulas in the metric view.</li>
# MAGIC <li><strong>"Can Power BI or Tableau use it?"</strong> Yes: Tableau and Sigma through custom SQL or BI compatibility mode, Power BI through semantic models (Private Preview) or custom SQL. Excel and Google Sheets are supported too.</li>
# MAGIC <li><strong>"Performance?"</strong> Materialization can pre-compute aggregations, and queries are rewritten automatically.</li>
# MAGIC <li><strong>"Local vs UC metric view?"</strong> Local is a dashboard-only sandbox. UC is the governed, shared definition.</li>
# MAGIC </ul>
# MAGIC </div>

